WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.980
Fuuka...

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.680
When did you get here?

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.270
I would have come to pick you up, 
if you'd let me know you were coming.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.680
Sorry.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.030
I was going to surprise you.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.200
You surprised me.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:14.990
Are you on vacation?

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.700
How long can you stay?

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.460
I decided to work at Tingarla, too!

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:24.580
No way!

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:36.000
I asked Grams where you'd moved 
and secretly moved in here.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.010
I thought I'd surprise you.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.470
We're neighbors starting today, huh?

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.970
This is the Chief Attendant, Garandu.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.490
It's <i>Garandou</i>.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.320
Nice to meet you.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.150
I'm Miyazawa Fuuka.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.910
I'm sorry for arriving two days late.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.840
No worries.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.560
Your flight was delayed. 
There was nothing you could do.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.120
Well, here's your appointment.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.630
Miyazawa Fuuka-san.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.930
You are assigned as attendant 
in the Aquatic Animals division.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:39.770
Yes, sir.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.640
You're one of us here at Tingarla now.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.940
Let's make every day a happy one.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.270
<b>Miyazawa Fuuka</b>

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.270
<b>As of April 1, 2022, you are assigned 
as Attendant in the Aquatic Animals division.</b>

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.270
Marketing?

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.980
Product PR in marketing.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:55.570
Is that right...

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.820
I never even imagined I'd be working 
as anything other than an attendant.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:05.410
I thought I was through, but since I get 
to work with you, I'm going to try my best.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.630
Yeah.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.830
Do you know what
aquatic animals we have?

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.000
Yes.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.130
Cape penguins, California sea lions, 
and Asian short-clawed otters, right?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.220
Yup.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.510
I heard you were taking care 
of Cape penguins at Gama Gama.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.180
Yes.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.660
That's perfect.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.470
I'll have you be in charge 
of the penguins, then.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:29.890
Yes, sir.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.500
Huh? Miyazawa-san?

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.390
I had a look at your résumé.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.120
You were an idol, huh?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.240
Yes!

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.640
I see.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.750
So why did you decide 
to work at an aquarium?

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.750
It's because I had the opportunity 
to work at Gama Gama last year.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.880
Kukuru-san, Kukuru-san!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.080
Yes?

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.860
That new employee who
just got hired is <i>so</i> pretty.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.620
You mean Fuuka?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.360
You know her?

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.100
Yes.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.350
I heard she was assigned as an attendant.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.680
In charge of penguins.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.170
Oh, really?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:18.770
Plankton.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.190
Yes, sir!

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.320
We're doing a test run of the
behind-the-scenes tour in a week.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.860
One week?!

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.830
Get it set up.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:27.490
But...

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.780
What?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.840
We just opened.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.340
I think we should wait until everyone's
settled in before we do any events.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.760
A lot of aquariums are doing 
behind-the-scenes tours right now.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.000
Why is that?

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.320
To have the guests appreciate aquariums?

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.880
That's part of it, obviously.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.000
What else?

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.270
Advertising.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.680
Advertising...

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.930
We won't see results immediately, 
but it's an effective way

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.780
to encourage word-of-mouth advertising 
on social media, and to get repeat customers.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.900
In other words, it's part of our job 
of generating Tingarla fans.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.410
That's all from me.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.500
Huh?

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:21.860
Okay.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.120
I'm Miyazawa Fuuka. 
I'll be working here starting today.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.010
Cape Penguin Team chief Haebaru Chiyu.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.020
I haven't seen you since Gama Gama.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:37.900
Right.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.480
I look forward to working with you.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.480
Yonekura Marina.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.730
Let's have fun here at work!

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.290
Nice to meet you.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.780
Were you brought in 
by the Gama Gama director, too?

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:49.740
Yes.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.060
I see.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.170
How long were you at Gama Gama?

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.370
A month.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.180
One month?

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.360
What other experience do you have?

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.500
I don't have any.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:07.380
I'm sure I'll be deficient in some ways, 
but I'll work hard to learn the job.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.310
For starters, I'll have you take a test.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:12.260
A test?

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.390
We have twenty Cape penguins here.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.360
Please memorize all their names

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.770
from the colors of their flipper
bands and their ID numbers.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:27.300
Acquaint yourself with each of their faces, 
personalities, and relationships.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.780
We'll be giving them food supplements.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.540
You can't do your job 
if you can't tell them apart.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.920
I couldn't tell them apart at first, either.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:40.420
It's easy once you get used to it, though.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.040
Got it?

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.140
Yes. Understood.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:02.960
Kukuru, we're holding a welcome-back party 
for Fuuka-chan at Ohana tonight.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.890
I invited the others already.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:06.790
Okay, got it.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.190
The behind-the-scenes tour?

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.400
Yeah.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.290
The one that we had to
cancel the dry run for.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.210
We're going straight into it.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.080
Break a leg.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.440
You don't <i>actually</i> care.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.330
Boo hoo.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.730
Haebaru-san.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.170
Sorry to interrupt your work.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:34.380
Per my email, we're going to be running 
the behind-the-scenes tour in a week.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.330
Understood.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.270
I look forward to it!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.790
But could we leave the penguins out?

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.770
But the penguins are really popular.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.400
I get that the behind-the-scenes tour 
is an important project.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.990
But it's too difficult right now.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:54.740
You were an attendant. You must know.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.870
Oh, we can't do it.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.740
We have too many newbies.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.500
We're barely making it 
through our day-to-day.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.880
It's your job to make arrangements 
with each section.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.210
Take responsibility.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.380
As I said...

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.220
Assistant Director!

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.000
What does he want me to do?

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.280
Come on.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.880
It's Fuuka-chan's welcome-back party.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:26.810
Buck up.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.810
Sorry.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:31.120
Long time, Fuuka-chan!

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.460
Udon-chan!

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.410
I'm glad to see you again!

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.280
I just really wanted to be back.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.910
Cheers!

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.410
Yakamashi Kuuya isn't here.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:44.670
He has a late shift today.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.900
Ah.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.750
I feel like a sardine 
in a school of horse mackerel.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.200
What does that mean? Um...

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.510
Oh, this is Higa Eiji-san. 
He's with us on the fish team.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.280
I heard it's a meeting 
of former Gama Gama employees,

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.560
so I thought I should pass 
on the invitation.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.380
But I was caught and hauled to shore.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.850
Hauled to shore?

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:10.040
I heard some people are saying 
the Gama Gama people are creating a faction.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.380
That's not true at all.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.950
I was working at the Tourism Association.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.570
I see.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:22.320
And our star for the night, Fuuka-chan, was
 working part-time at Gama Gama last summer.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:25.920
And now, she's a full-time
employee at Tingarla.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.790
From an idol to an attendant...

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:31.080
It's as though a smolt has grown 
into a salmon.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:33.090
She's not like those fish 
with different names based on growth.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.920
How did you know she's an idol?

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.880
My boss told me.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.490
Oh, Garandou-san.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.510
That guy's so laid-back.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.930
In a good way.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:45.640
In a good way?

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.300
Here you are!

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:53.530
So, Fuuka-chan, 
how did you end up back here?

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.880
Working at Gama Gama made me feel 
that an aquarium's the right place for me.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:04.370
So I decided to talk to Gramps, 
and he hooked me up with Tingarla.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.680
I see.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.590
That's why you said 
you got a diving license.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.280
Diving?

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:14.560
I don't have much knowledge or experience, 
so I wanted to find a way to be useful.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:18.080
You sure do work for your goals.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.130
Nah.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.510
From whitebait to an anchovy, then.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.580
Enough about fish already!

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.710
Never.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.990
You're such a grown-up, Fuuka.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:34.270
I'm such a child. I got jealous 
when I heard you became an attendant.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.140
That's not true.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.120
No, I need to work hard.

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:48.560
I want to do my job properly for now 
and go back to attendant work someday.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.120
That's my goal.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:54.000
I still love living things.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:12.850
<b>Konpeito
No. 12 8 years
Ring color:</b>

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:12.850
<b>Daifuku
No. 15 6 years
Ring color:</b>

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.860
That one's Konpeito.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.610
Was his big sister Hina-arare?

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.680
The one that's always in the water is...

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:28.450
They must be stressed out 
from having just come to a new aquarium.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.710
I'll take care of you 
so you can feel at home sooner.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:37.000
<b>Penguin Chaser</b>

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:56.230
Fine, I'll cooperate.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.170
Really?

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.240
Chief Garandou told me to take it on.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.700
I can't say "no."

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.450
Huh? Okay.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.250
I'm not going to deal 
with customers, though.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:08.940
Okay.

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:10.120
I'll do that.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.080
Bye.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:15.530
Well, at least I got an "okay."

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:22.320
Th-Thank you very much for participating 
in the Aquarium Tingarla Behind-the-scenes Tour.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:26.080
Kukuru-san, you have to smile more.

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.220
You're going to scare the guests away.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:33.040
Thank you for helping 
with the rehearsal.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.310
Not at all.

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:38.300
Are you going to be 
the tour guide yourself, Kukuru-san?

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.940
I figured I'd do that at first.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:46.940
We use this machine to clean the water 
and return it to the tanks.

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:48.060
Wow.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:50.830
I never knew aquarium water gets dirty.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:54.200
This is the heart of Tingarla.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.710
We watch over all the tanks 
twenty-four hours a day.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.710
You can see the fish.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:06.200
We prepare different feed 
for different fish.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.090
Look at that!

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:14.780
We're above the main aquarium.

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:18.690
Let's feed the fish.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:26.450
They're really going at it!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.450
The penguins are so cute.

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:35.080
I wish I could show off the penguins 
up close at the end.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:49.340
Azuki and Ohagi are fighting again.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:54.520
That one's always in the corner.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.360
Uirou, was it?

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.920
That just about does it.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.900
Aquariums are pretty fun, huh?

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:09.180
Oh, I just work here because
I live pretty close.

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:12.800
I wasn't especially interested in aquariums.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.410
Really?

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:18.750
But looking around 
has been surprisingly fun!

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.550
I know, right?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.740
Despite what the Assistant Director said,

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:31.550
I still want people to come to the behind-the-scenes
tour and fall in love with aquariums.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.760
So I'm going to work hard!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.640
You're so amusing, Kukuru-san.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:45.030
I've coordinated with attendants, 
facilities, and customer staff.

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:50.220
And I checked over the itinerary 
with Maeda-san's help.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.860
What about announcements?

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.620
I've already arranged to have an announcement 
to be posted on our website.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:56.780
Fair enough.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.310
Just...

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.750
I haven't been able to get 
the Penguin team to agree.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.420
Damn it.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:05.480
Whatever.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.880
We'll do it without penguins this time.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.880
But I think people will
appreciate the penguins.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.220
Which is it?!

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.550
I'll go plead with them again!

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.460
Hey, where's Haebaru-san?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.300
She went home already.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.740
Want to talk to Marina-san?

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:24.270
Okay.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:26.300
Marina-san.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:27.280
Yeah?

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.140
This is Misakino Kukuru-san from marketing.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:31.210
Misakino.

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:31.980
Um...

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:35.210
Oh, is this about the behind-the-scenes tour?

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:35.910
Yes.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.990
The behind-the-scenes tour sounds great.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:41.670
It's a chance to talk 
to the guests directly.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:45.150
Then would you mind being the guide, 
if we can get it working?

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.670
I'd love to.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.650
I'm looking forward to it.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:54.020
Everyone, those ones over there 
are the Cape penguins!

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:57.390
We haven't gotten the go-ahead 
from Penguins yet, though.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.200
Right.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:02.190
I'm sure Chiyu-san will agree eventually.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.530
I'll do anything I can to help.

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:06.730
Never give up!

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.400
<i>Nunca te rindas</i>!

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.200
I'm not giving up.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.530
Good, good.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.240
I'll come back to ask Haebaru-san again.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.370
You're done now, right?

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.060
Let's go home together.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:20.280
I'm going to stay for a bit longer.

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:22.140
I have to memorize for the test.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:23.250
Test?

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.760
You made that, huh?

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:28.680
Yeah.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:30.280
Can I see?

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.500
I'm not...

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.390
You won't remember if you keep looking.

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:34.380
Okay.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:36.510
Who's that?

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.390
Male, number sixteen... Kusamochi-kun?

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.420
Close.

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:43.110
It's Kashiwamochi-kun.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:50.530
They aren't used to this environment yet.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.780
Right.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:55.910
Of course.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.870
Female, number eleven, Sakuramochi.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.580
And who's her partner?

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:09.710
This one!

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:10.420
Dorayaki.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.740
Bingo!

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:15.510
Okay, next.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.350
Fuuka!

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:31.570
Are you ready?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:32.730
Yes!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.030
Go!

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:37.410
Okaki.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:38.780
Daifuku.

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:40.410
Kashiwamochi.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:43.050
Popo the Curious.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:46.160
The happily married Sakuramochi and Dorayaki.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.420
Muchi the Hungry.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.590
Konpeito and his big sister, Hina-arare.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.440
That one in the corner is Uirou.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:56.720
Those ones fighting are Ohagi and Azuki.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:59.220
Chimaki, Nerikiri, Chitoseame.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:01.720
Rakugan, Youkan, Amanatto.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.900
Kurimanju, and...

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.480
Zundamochi-kun!

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.230
Correct!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:10.610
Perfect!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.680
You did it, Fuuka!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.260
You pass.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:18.110
Good job memorizing them so quickly.

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:22.300
Thank you!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:24.990
Haebaru-san.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:26.750
Yes?

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:31.500
Could you please reconsider your decision 
on the behind-the-scenes tour?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.660
I really want to show off the penguins.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.250
Chiyu-san, I can handle it.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.810
The penguins here are new.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.510
A lot of them are still agitated.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.770
That's why you said 
it would be difficult, right?

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:51.650
I don't think we can feed them yet,

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:55.400
but I'll be mindful to make sure 
the guests stay a certain distance away.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.940
We'll be careful not to
stress the penguins out.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.260
Please!

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:04.540
If it's only to observe feeding time.

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:05.770
Then!

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.660
But if something happens to the penguins, 
we're calling it off immediately.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:10.500
Okay!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:18.130
<b>Time: Approx. 60 minutes</b>

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.130
<b>Capacity: 8 people per group</b>

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.130
<b>Meeting Time: 1:30 PM</b>

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.130
<b>Aquarium Tingarla 
Behind-the-scenes Tour</b>

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:18.130
Today's the big day, huh?

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.130
<b>Take a peek behind the scenes!</b>

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.130
<b>Free entry</b>

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:21.130
Thank you for all your help today.

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:22.970
Not at all.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:26.950
But it's time, and no one's shown up yet.

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:29.230
Pardon me!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.240
Can I still join the behind-the-scenes tour?

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:34.120
Yes!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.300
Yay!

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.440
Thank you.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:46.030
The back area is an important place. 
It's where we take care of the animals.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:52.040
This is the machine 
that always keeps the water clean.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:56.420
This is the room 
where we watch over the animals.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:01.950
We're right above the main aquarium.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:03.680
Look at all of them!

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.050
It's a manta ray!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.110
There, you must be hungry.

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:15.230
Penguin food!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:21.510
We put supplements in the penguin food, 
so that they can be healthy every day.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:27.780
Hina-arare and Konpeitou over there 
are sister and brother.

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:32.600
That was fun!

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.290
I want to come back 
to see the penguins again!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.640
We'll be waiting.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.290
Thank you.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.890
Our kids really enjoyed it.

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.350
I had fun, too.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.760
I'm glad.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.050
Please enjoy the main facility as well.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.540
Thank you.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.060
Thank you.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:51.830
Bye-bye.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.880
They liked it.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:56.060
Yeah!

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.820
Just one group?

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.320
Ridiculous.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.340
Yes, sir...

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.570
Come up with better ways 
to attract customers.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:05.320
Yes, sir!

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:12.950
I'm going to leave you 
in the dust someday!

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:49.960
Curse you, Assistant Director.

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:52.930
But the guests had a nice time, right?

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:54.090
Yup.

00:22:54.090 --> 00:22:55.420
It's all thanks to you, Fuuka.

00:22:55.420 --> 00:22:58.560
What? But I didn't do anything.

00:22:58.850 --> 00:23:02.250
No, it's because you passed the test

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:04.650
that Haebaru-san gave in.

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:06.900
You think so?

00:23:08.680 --> 00:23:11.610
I need to work harder like you.

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:14.490
I can do my best when you're around.

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:17.120
Kukuru.

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:18.420
Hm?

00:23:18.420 --> 00:23:19.620
You see...

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:23.140
Ever since I heard that
you were going to Tingarla

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:25.940
I was determined to come back here.

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:30.620
I came back because you're here, Kukuru.

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:33.770
Well, I'm glad you're here.
